kipedia.org/wiki/Tama_(cat</a>)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morris_the_Cat\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Morris_the_Cat.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morris_the_Cat\" target=\"_blank\"> Morris the Cat - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morris_the_Cat\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morris_the_Cat </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Would be awesome to have familiars like these<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T16:27:37-08:00","id":1060332,"title":"","content":"Void Engineers doing some climate postcognition in a <a href=\"http://pvtimes.com/news/researchers-diving-deep-devil-s-hole-study-climate-history\" target=\"_blank\">crazy, adventurous location</a>: Devil's Hole in Death Valley. <br /> Cavern diving is some scary stuff. Diving to 300' is crazier still. I wouldn't mind roleplaying this campaign, but you wouldn't get me to go on this adventure for real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T19:34:08-08:00","id":1060386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048017-mage-in-the-real-world?p=1048357#post1048357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nop, he just say that he's &quot;sure&quot; the technocracy it's capable of atrocities. And that it wouldn't be below them to make a few &quot;traditional&quot; human sacrifices if to make the trads look bad. Saying that in no way implies that the Traditions can't do as bad or worse.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's below all of them, but many Technocrats are going to complain about such an extremist action as to kill people to frame the Trads. They can say it's an unnecessary and wastefull loss of human live and a mockery of the Union's mission of protecting the masses, they can even say that it's a violation of the Principles of Damian (the one about protecting the masses). The retort would be...well, the same that the Progenitors get when the Syndicate sells defective homeopaty to bastardize Traditional belief...that &quot;it's for the greater good&quot; (the prefered way of evading the technoctatic law).</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically that line is &quot;Shepherd the Masses.&quot; Not &quot;Protect the Masses.&quot; Is protection implied? Certainly. But Shepherds also kill members of their flock when needed.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that the &quot;Terrorism&quot; skill appeared in the Guide to the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T04:06:43-08:00","id":1060470,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-39193347\" target=\"_blank\">Literal rabbit-hole leads to Knights Templar cave.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T10:42:07-08:00","id":1060570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GogariGlenRoss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048017-mage-in-the-real-world?p=1060470#post1060470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-39193347\" target=\"_blank\">Literal rabbit-hole leads to Knights Templar cave.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Couple points here.<br /> <br /> First, the article mentions the site being supposedly used for &quot;black magic rites&quot; in the modern day. This could be a cover story by the Technocracy to feed into biases against mysticism. The Union did likely have a hand in anti-witch hysteria throughout the centuries, and continues to do so. The Templars could have continued using the site up until it was sealed. Alternatively, it could have actually been used by Infernalists or Nephandi, looking to subvert a sacred space for their own vile ends.<br /> <br /> Second, the article says that while it's claimed to have been built by the Templars, examiners date it to the 18th or 19th centuries, after the Templars dissolved. This, too, could just be Technocrat propaganda, experts being induced to claim it to be newer for the sake of, again, undermining mysticism. Then again, in the WoD, the Templars have continued to exist (covertly) into the modern day. So it's hardly a stretch to think they might have carved out hidden &quot;chantries&quot;, so they could worship and operate in secret. Who knows how many sites like this one litter the World of Darkness, just under the surface (in this case literally)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T13:08:29-08:00","id":1060623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.mid-day.com/articles/wanted-man-taunts-cops-iconic-hide-and